Ladybird reads a clipboard’s plain-text types in turn, the UTF-8 ones
first, and keeps the first text that one of them answers, as a single
text/plain. Chromium does the same on X11: X11ClipboardOzone reads plain
text in one request over the targets that GetTextAtomsFrom() lists,
UTF8_STRING first and text/plain;charset=utf-8 last, after STRING, TEXT,
and text/plain. Firefox’s nsClipboard reads its one text flavor with
GetClipboardText(), through GTK’s text request. From reading the
sources; a reporter of the Bitwarden reports found that Brave, Chromium,
and Firefox all paste from it.
